AltoRewardsOracle::Constructor()
├── given invalid inputs
│   ├── when addressInAndOutUni length is not 2
│   │   └── it should revert with AltoRewardsOracleInvalidInput
│   ├── when owner is zero address
│   │   └── it should revert with OwnableInvalidOwner
│   ├── when twap period is invalid
│   │   └── it should revert with UniswapUtilsInvalidTwapPeriod
│   ├── when circuit uniswap parameters are invalid
│   │   └── it should revert with ModuleUniswapMultiInvalidInput
│   └── when circuit chainlink parameters are invalid
│       └── it should revert with ModuleChainlinkMultiInvalidInput
└── given valid inputs
    ├── when valid parameters provided
    │   ├── it should set IN_BASE correctly based on in-currency decimals
    │   ├── it should set OUT_BASE correctly based on out-currency decimals
    │   ├── it should set UNI_FINAL_CURRENCY correctly
    │   ├── it should set description correctly
    │   ├── it should set priceUpdateCooldownPeriod correctly
    │   ├── it should set owner correctly
    │   ├── it should set twap period correctly
    │   ├── it should set circuit uniswap correctly
    │   ├── it should set circuit uni is multiplied correctly
    │   ├── it should set circuit chainlink correctly
    │   ├── it should set circuit chain is multiplied correctly
    │   ├── it should set stale period correctly
    │   ├── it should initialize lastPriceUpdateTimestamp to zero
    │   ├── it should initialize cachedPrice to zero
    │   └── it should emit PriceUpdateCooldownPeriodUpdated event
    └── when tokens have different decimal places
        ├── it should handle when in-currency token has 6 decimal places and out-currency token has 8 decimal places correctly
